    "schema": "Article",
    "bluf": "This log helps you write down a late or missed period with the context around it: illness, stress, travel, medicine changes, and pregnancy-test notes if relevant. It cannot tell you why your period is late or whether you are pregnant. If you feel unsafe, very sick, or worried, ask for care before you finish the log.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "Is this medical advice?",
        "a": "No. It is a notes and question-prep tool. Ask a clinician about pain, heavy bleeding, missed periods, or pregnancy concerns."
      },
      {
        "q": "Should I write every detail about stress or travel?",
        "a": "No. Write only what may help explain timing. Short notes like 'work deadline' or 'overnight flight' are enough."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can Floriva tell me why my period is late?",
        "a": "No. Floriva can help you keep short cycle notes on your device. It does not diagnose the cause or tell you if you are pregnant."
      }
    ],
    "answers": [
      {
        "question": "What should I track when my period is late or missed?",
        "answer": "Write the expected period date, last full period date, any bleeding or spotting, and context such as stress, illness, travel, sleep, and medicine changes. Add pregnancy-test notes only if that is part of your question."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can this log tell me why my period is late?",
        "answer": "No. A log cannot tell you the cause. NHS and MedlinePlus both list many possible contexts for late or missed periods, including pregnancy, stress, illness, travel, weight change, exercise, perimenopause, and some medicines."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can this log tell me if I am pregnant?",
        "answer": "No. It cannot tell you if you are pregnant or rule it out, even alongside a negative test. Follow the test label and ask a clinician if timing or results feel unclear."
      }
    ],
