    "schema": "Article",
    "bluf": "This kit gives you a one-cycle BBT chart, a disruption log, a cervical mucus and LH test strip tracker, an ovulation symptom tracker, and a chart review checklist. It teaches tracking basics. It does not diagnose ovulation, pregnancy, or a health problem, and it does not replace fertility awareness method training.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "Is this medical advice?",
        "a": "No. It teaches tracking basics. Ask a clinician about fever, pain, heavy bleeding, missed periods, sudden cycle changes, or fertility concerns."
      },
      {
        "q": "Do I need LH tests or BBT to use this kit?",
        "a": "No. Use whichever sections match the signs you track. Combining signs gives a stronger pattern than any single sign alone."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can Floriva confirm ovulation for me?",
        "a": "No. Floriva can hold cycle dates, symptoms, and fertility signs on your device. It does not diagnose ovulation or replace method-specific training."
      }
    ],
    "answers": [
      {
        "question": "What should I track to understand ovulation?",
        "answer": "Track basal body temperature, cervical mucus, LH test results if you use them, mid-cycle pain, spotting, and libido. No single sign proves ovulation by itself; a pattern across several cycles is more useful."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does a positive LH test or a BBT rise prove ovulation happened?",
        "answer": "No. FDA says home ovulation urine tests detect the LH surge about 1 to 1.5 days before ovulation but do not confirm an egg was released. BBT confirms ovulation only after the fact, through a sustained temperature rise across several days."
      },
      {
        "question": "How long does it take to learn fertility awareness charting?",
        "answer": "Most practitioners report needing three to six cycles before feeling confident reading their charts. If you use FAM for contraception, standard advice is to use a backup method during that learning period."
      }
    ],
    "definitions": [
      {
        "term": "BBT",
        "definition": "Basal body temperature. It is your resting temperature, taken right after waking, before getting out of bed."
      },
      {
        "term": "LH surge",
        "definition": "A rise in luteinizing hormone that often happens before ovulation. LH strips detect this surge."
      },
      {
        "term": "Cervical mucus",
        "definition": "Fluid from the cervix that changes in texture and amount across the cycle. Egg-white-like mucus often shows near peak fertility."
      },
      {
        "term": "Thermal shift",
        "definition": "A sustained rise in BBT across three or more days that can confirm ovulation already happened."
      },
      {
        "term": "Uncertainty flag",
        "definition": "A short mark or note that says a reading may be missing, late, unclear, or affected by something else."
      }
    ],
