    "schema": "Article",
    "bluf": "This PMDD quiz is a private self-check. It does not diagnose PMDD. It helps you look for pattern signals: symptoms that rise before a period, ease after bleeding starts, affect daily life, and show up across more than one cycle.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "Do I need to enter an email?",
        "a": "No. This self-check is meant to be read and used on the page."
      },
      {
        "q": "What if symptoms happen all month?",
        "a": "That still deserves care. It may point to another mood or health condition, or a condition that gets worse before a period. Track the full month and bring it to a clinician."
      },
      {
        "q": "What should I track after this quiz?",
        "a": "Track daily mood, anxiety, anger, low mood, body symptoms, function, bleeding, and the first day symptoms ease. Use at least 2 cycles if you can."
      }
    ],
    "answers": [
      {
        "question": "Is there a PMDD quiz with no email?",
        "answer": "Yes. This page is a no-email PMDD self-check. It does not save your answers or diagnose you. Use it to decide what to track and what to bring to a clinician."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can a PMDD quiz diagnose PMDD?",
        "answer": "No. PMDD needs clinical review. Daily symptom ratings across at least 2 cycles are often used because memory alone can miss the timing."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are the main PMDD pattern signals?",
        "answer": "The strongest signals are mood symptoms before a period, symptom relief soon after bleeding starts, daily life disruption, and the same pattern across more than one cycle."
      },
      {
        "question": "When should PMDD symptoms be urgent?",
        "answer": "Get urgent help if you may hurt yourself, may hurt someone else, feel unsafe, or cannot get through the day safely."
      }
    ],
