    "schema": "Article",
    "bluf": "Kindara was a subscription-based fertility tracking app that charged for BBT charting and fertility awareness method (FAM) tools. The app was discontinued, and users lost access to their tracking data stored on Kindara's servers. This is the hidden cost of cloud-dependent health tracking: your data's existence depends on a company's continued operation.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "Why did Kindara shut down",
        "a": "Kindara was acquired and the product was eventually discontinued. The specific business reasons are not fully public, but the outcome for users is clear: the service ended, and cloud-stored data went with it."
      },
      {
        "q": "What happened to the Wink thermometer",
        "a": "The Wink was a Bluetooth BBT thermometer designed to pair with Kindara's app. When Kindara was discontinued, Wink owners lost their companion app. The thermometer still reads temperatures, but the charting software it was built for no longer exists. This is hardware lock-in risk in practice."
      },
      {
        "q": "How does Floriva prevent this problem",
        "a": "Floriva keeps core records on your device in local storage. If Floriva ever stopped operating, your local records would be less dependent on company servers. Floriva also includes export tools; check the current app for exact fields and formats."
      }
    ],
    "answers": [
      {
        "question": "How much did Kindara cost",
        "answer": "Kindara offered a free tier with basic charting and a premium subscription with full FAM tools and Wink thermometer integration. Exact pricing varied over the app's lifetime. The app has been discontinued, so current pricing is not available."
      },
      {
        "question": "What happened to Kindara user data",
        "answer": "When Kindara was discontinued, its servers went offline. Users who stored their cycle data on Kindara's cloud infrastructure lost access to that data. Some users may have exported data before the shutdown if the feature was available, but many did not."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I still use Kindara",
        "answer": "No. Kindara has been discontinued. The app is no longer available for download, and the servers that stored user data are offline. Former Kindara users need to find an alternative app and start their tracking history from scratch unless they exported data before the shutdown."
      }
    ],
