    "bluf": "Natural Cycles is FDA-cleared contraception stored on a cloud server. Before you switch, you need to cancel the subscription (separate from deleting the account), export your temperature data, delete the account, and file a GDPR erasure request. This guide walks through each step in the right order.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "Does Natural Cycles delete my data when I close my account?",
        "a": "In-app account deletion removes your active data. Backup copies may persist until you file a GDPR Article 17 erasure request with privacy@naturalcycles.com. Natural Cycles is a Swedish company and GDPR-compliant, so they have 30 days to respond and must purge backup data upon a valid erasure request. Cancel your subscription before deleting the account to avoid continued billing."
      },
      {
        "q": "Will I lose my temperature history when I leave Natural Cycles?",
        "a": "Not if you export before deleting. Natural Cycles exports include your basal body temperature logs, cycle dates, and fertility status entries. BBT history is time-intensive to collect and not recoverable from memory. The export file is your temperature record. Download it before any other step. If you are moving to an on-device tracker that supports BBT logging, you can reference the export to reconstruct your temperature patterns."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can Natural Cycles data be subpoenaed?",
        "a": "Natural Cycles is a Swedish company, which provides some jurisdictional distance from US legal process. However, cloud-based data can in principle be subject to legal requests via mutual legal assistance treaties between countries. On-device storage removes this risk because there is no readable central copy to produce. If you are switching for legal safety reasons, moving to an on-device tracker eliminates the server-side exposure entirely."
      },
      {
        "q": "How do I cancel Natural Cycles billing without deleting my account?",
        "a": "If you subscribed through the Apple App Store, cancel through iPhone Settings, then your name, then Subscriptions. If you subscribed through Google Play, cancel through Play Store subscriptions. If you subscribed directly through naturalcycles.com, log in and cancel through Settings, then Subscription. Cancellation must happen at the billing source. Deleting the Natural Cycles app or account does not automatically cancel subscription billing."
      }
    ],
