        "answer": "Implantation bleeding is typically light, often just a few spots of blood on underwear or when wiping. The color is usually pink or brownish rather than bright red. It does not involve clots and does not increase in flow the way a period does. Most people who experience it describe it as noticeably lighter than their lightest period day."
