    "steps": [
      {
        "title": "Export your cycle history",
        "content": "In Clue, tap the menu icon (three lines), then Settings, then Data Management, then Export Data. Clue emails a download link within 24-48 hours. The export is a CSV covering cycle dates, symptom tags, and tracked categories."
      },
      {
        "title": "Delete your account (not just the app)",
        "content": "Open Settings, go to Privacy, then tap Delete Account. Clue is GDPR-based, so the deletion flow includes explicit confirmation steps. Uninstalling alone leaves your data on Clue's servers in Berlin."
      },
      {
        "title": "Verify deletion",
        "content": "Wait 24-48 hours. Try to log in with your old Clue credentials. A successful deletion returns an 'account not found' error. If login still works, the request did not complete and you should repeat step 2."
      },
      {
        "title": "Submit a CCPA/GDPR data deletion request",
        "content": "Email data-requests@helloclue.com. Subject: 'GDPR Data Deletion Request.' State your Clue account email and invoke your right under GDPR Article 17 (right to erasure) or CCPA Section 1798.105 if you are in California. Clue must respond within 30 days (GDPR) or 45 days (CCPA)."
      },
      {
        "title": "Choose your replacement tracker",
        "content": "Privacy-first options: Floriva (paid, polished, local-first with optional encrypted sync), Euki (free, nonprofit-maintained, local-only), Drip (free, open-source, community-maintained, local-only). All three reduce company-held readable cycle records."
      },
      {
        "title": "Start logging in the new app",
        "content": "Open the Clue CSV in any spreadsheet. Enter your last 3-6 cycle start dates into the new tracker. Most prediction algorithms need 2-3 recorded cycles to stabilize, so seeding from Clue's history avoids a warm-up period of less accurate forecasts."
      }
    ],
