        "question": "What happened with Premom and the FTC?",
        "answer": "On May 17, 2023, the FTC filed its second-ever Health Breach Notification Rule enforcement action against Easy Healthcare Corporation (Case 1:23-cv-03107, N.D. Illinois). The complaint established that Premom shared menstrual cycle and fertility data with Google and AppsFlyer through descriptive custom events. From 2018 through 2020, Premom also shared device identifiers and precise geolocation with two Chinese companies: Umeng, an Alibaba subsidiary, and Jiguang (also known as Aurora Mobile). The settlement imposed a $100,000 federal civil penalty and $100,000 to state AGs in Connecticut, Oregon, and D.C. Easy Healthcare was permanently banned from sharing health data for advertising and required to notify affected users directly."
