      {
        "question": "Do I need to log symptoms every day for accurate predictions",
        "answer": "No. Cycle predictions are based on period start dates, not daily symptom logs. Logging symptoms is useful for identifying patterns (like PMS timing) but is not required for the core prediction to work. All five apps generate predictions from start dates alone."
      },
      {
        "question": "What does 'no surveillance' mean for a period tracker",
        "answer": "It means the app does not embed advertising or analytics SDKs that send user behavior to third parties, does not require an account that ties cycle data to an email or phone number, and does not sync data to company-controlled servers by default. The 2021 FTC action against Flo documented exactly the kind of SDK-layer data sharing that 'no surveillance' apps are built to avoid. Health data flowed to Facebook, Google Analytics, and AppsFlyer despite policy language to the contrary."
      }
